From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Feb 2026 13:13:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: exclude dnf5.log from chroot_scan output in rpmbuild

DNF5 unconditionally writes verbose debug/info logs to dnf5.log (the
DNF4 debuglevel option is not implemented in DNF5), producing thousands
of lines of noise that bury actual build errors in CI output. Exclude it
from the tar dump while keeping it available in the chroot_scan.tar.gz
artifact for manual inspection if needed.
---
 task/rpmbuild.yaml | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/task/rpmbuild.yaml b/task/rpmbuild.yaml
index 804a3ee..c732427 100644
--- a/task/rpmbuild.yaml
+++ b/task/rpmbuild.yaml
@@ -189,9 +189,14 @@ spec:
           || success=false
         fi
 
-        # display dnf logs (no matter the mock exit status), and propagate the
-        # mock failure (terminates the whole script)
-        remote_cmd tar xfO $HOMEDIR/results/chroot_scan.tar.gz
+        # Display chroot_scan logs (no matter the mock exit status), excluding
+        # dnf5.log which is extremely verbose and buries useful error output.
+        # DNF5 unconditionally writes detailed debug/info logs to dnf5.log
+        # (the DNF4 debuglevel option is not implemented in DNF5), so this
+        # file contains thousands of lines of noise (plugin loading, librepo
+        # internals, RPM callback open/close for every package, etc.).
+        # The full dnf5.log is still available in chroot_scan.tar.gz if needed.
+        remote_cmd tar xfO $HOMEDIR/results/chroot_scan.tar.gz --exclude='*/dnf5.log'
         $success
 
         resultdir="$workdir/results/$arch"
